{"skill":{"slug":"proactive-agent-skill","displayName":"Proactive Agent Skill"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1772382944971,"changelog":"- Initial release of proactive-agent skill (v1.0.0).\n- Implements core WAL Protocol for state persistence and recovery.\n- Introduces working buffer for critical context logging and memory compaction.\n- Adds support for proactive heartbeats and autonomous/prompted cron automation.\n- Provides configuration templates and best practices for proactive, self-improving agent design.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5167,"sha256":"93c2fd84bec00a72eb52ea9b30c3af008a8fc60191c4fdae64b73e35997aeb7e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2164,"sha256":"78635c01dbca9999c97858ee2d44a039dc9ecbe86ee106a64fb8b29e144f6ab9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789094648529,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c1c0c97857d4b50f18fa340f2f51f9e55f7161c7ed327a3d0bb550c4bc19e6a9","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c1c0c97857d4b50f18fa340f2f51f9e55f7161c7ed327a3d0bb550c4bc19e6a9","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780089732940},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":58,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789094648529},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill openly teaches proactive automation, but it also encourages persistent memory, broad monitoring, and unattended scheduled agent runs without enough user-control safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The recommended heartbeats and crons may repeatedly use whatever OpenClaw tools and integrations are available in the user's environment, while the artifact gives little guidance on least-privilege accounts, scoped integrations, audit logs, or disable/removal controls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected package is a Markdown-only skill with no bundled executable scripts, dependencies, install hooks, or remote payload retrieval instructions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill uses broad triggers like routine checks and scheduled tasks, and it does not clearly require per-source consent, redaction, review before memory promotion, or limits on what email, calendar, conversation, and system data may be retained.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact explicitly recommends persistent Markdown memory files and cron entries invoking OpenClaw across sessions; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but under-scoped for the level of durable authority it creates.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The WAL, heartbeat, and cron capabilities fit the stated purpose of making an agent proactive, but the purpose itself involves sensitive behaviors such as email/calendar checks, long-term memory, and autonomous maintenance.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. It is not shown to contain hidden code or exfiltration, but only use it if you are prepared to explicitly limit which services it may check, keep memory files out of source control and sync systems, redact sensitive data, approve anything promoted to long-term memory, and manage any cron jobs with clear listing, pausing, and removal procedures.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Heartbeat checks are expected for a proactive-agent skill, but the artifact supports the concern because it names email, calendar, weather, and system checks without consent, scope, or retention controls.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad 'When to Use' examples make invocation scope unclear and are not necessary to the core proactive-agent architecture.\n[SSD-3] expected: Persistent working buffers and MEMORY.md fit the stated WAL purpose, but the artifact's 'captures every exchange' and 'log everything' language supports a privacy and memory-poisoning concern.\n[RA2] expected: Scheduled autonomous crons are an advertised feature, but the concrete cron examples create durable unattended OpenClaw execution without documented allowlists, approval gates, auditability, or removal guidance.\n[T06] expected: The static scan's persistence concern is supported by the artifact's cron examples that run OpenClaw tasks on recurring schedules across sessions.\n[T02] expected: The static scan's memory-poisoning concern is supported by instructions to store conversation-derived content, compact it, promote it to long-term memory, and restore from it later without trust labeling or user review.\n[T09] expected: The static scan's plaintext retention concern is supported by workspace Markdown memory files combined with email, calendar, conversation, and system-status collection examples.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789094648529}}}}}